  "title": "Hurricane Harvey - FARP and Refugee Evacuation",
  "description": "Airmen from the 71st Rescue Squadron and the 23rd Logistics Readiness Squadron conduct a Forward Area Refueling Point (FARP), refueling a Navy MH-60S Seahawk, and evacuate victims of Hurricane Harvey from Beaumont, Texas to Dallas, Texas. Hurricane Harvey formed in the Gulf of Mexico and made landfall in southeastern Texas, bringing record flooding and destruction to the region. U.S. military assets supported FEMA as well as state and local authorities in rescue and relief efforts.",
